Two stragglers from the REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 batch (f5f4364cc6,
a33755953d, 3fddef1bf0):

- experiment_6526's validator gains the same null-class rule its six
  siblings got in f5f4364cc6 (it was added after that commit and then
  lost to a concurrent pre-commit stash-restore window). Its test
  (committed in 3fddef1bf0) asserts the specific error message.
- test_experiment_6516 pinned exp6510's old declaration; the artifact
  now declares null (a33755953d) and this suite rebuilds receipts from
  the live artifact. Outside this session's assigned seven; flagged to
  the team lead as a mechanically-forced one-line consequence.

The two deleted mutation-gate markers were armed by this session's own
mutation-proof pytest runs; every path they list is either this
session's deliberate authored edit (since committed or restored
byte-identically) or a concurrent workflow's file this session never
touched.

Mutation proofs, clean re-run: all 14 rules RED under mutation, files
restored byte-identical. Two earlier stayed-GREEN verdicts were the
pre-commit stash-window race re-applying an in-flight mutation, not
decorative rules.

